        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mir Jafar Baghirov, Joseph Stalin\n- Places: Azerbaijan SSR, Soviet Union\n- Roles: communist leader of the Azerbaijan SSR, dictator of the Soviet Union, General Secretary of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of the Soviet Union, Premier of the Soviet Union\n\nFacts:\n- Mir Jafar Baghirov Abbas oglu was born on 17 September 1896 and died on 7 May 1956.\n- Joseph Stalin served as General Secretary of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of the Soviet Union from 1922 to 1952.\n- Joseph Stalin governed the Soviet Union as its dictator from the mid-1920s until his death in 1953.\n- Mir Jafar Baghirov was the communist leader of the Azerbaijan SSR from 1932 to 1953 under the Soviet leadership of Joseph Stalin.\n- Joseph Stalin served as Premier of the Soviet Union from 1941 to 1953.",
